item.description:
&lt;p&gt;PHP maintainers have &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-20-1&quot;&gt;released&lt;/a&gt; fixes for two critical vulnerabilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35 fix two critical vulnerabilities that can allow unauthenticated remote code execution. All PHP users are strongly encouraged to update immediately. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who is at risk: all PHP installations serving web requests, including PHP-FPM, Apache with mod_php, php-cgi, FrankenPHP and LiteSpeed. We consider the risk highest for mod_php, with a demonstrated exploit where an unauthenticated request can trigger the attack before any application code runs...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
